From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:25:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Card copies: the send-and-hash list can record its
 copies, one state change and its hash passes in three steps
 (VICTORY_CARD_SYNC_BATCH=1|alt, off by default)

Hand port of fork commit 6aed07804 (fork pull request #1227) onto b47. Copy by
copy the card went from copying to compute and back for every changed copy of
the list. With the switch every changed range is copied up first, then every
state change goes in one call, then every hash pass runs. Without it the list
is recorded copy by copy as before.

Kept from this line: the census count of what is sent, the hash size and the
group count as they are here (the fork's card meter, shot spans, card_hashed
and card_compare_groups are not on this line). The pull request's test comes
along, ignored (it needs the card).

(cherry picked by hand from 6aed07804)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
